      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Conflict kept: NC State 'keep soil slightly moist' vs UF/IFAS 'water when the top inch is dry' (UF stored, from_knowledge_verify). Toxicity: NC State rates it low, UF/IFAS says moderate to severe swelling in pets; the higher severity 2 is stored for cat and dog. Size is the upper end of NC State's range (up to 6 ft); the agent's choice. Interval: NC State 'keep soil slightly moist, and slow down on watering in winter'; Missouri Botanical Garden 'water regularly in growing season, reduce in fall to late winter'; UF/IFAS 'water when the top inch is dry'. The top inch of a 13 cm pot dries in about a week, so 7 (unchanged); the three agree on a moist-not-wet rule. Pot and season: 13 cm pot, bright indirect light, room temperature, growing season. Dry and wet tolerance days: no source gives days, left as before."
      },
